$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the isolation
experiments. Into a degassed supension of the pre-swelled gel catalyst
PdGel (25:1) (50 mg) in the 80% aq EtOH (50 °C, 20 mL) under Ar
atmosphere for 1 h, the arylboronic acid (3 mmol), potassium carbonate (6
mmol) and iodo- or bromoarene (2 mmol) were added. The reaction mixture
was heated to 50 °C (or 80 °C in the case of bromoarenes) under Ar
atmosphere (GC/MS monitoring). The reaction was quenched with 5% aq HCl,
extracted with ether, the organic layer was dried by magnesium sulfate
overnight, then after filtration the solution was evaporated. The crude
product was recrystallized from 20-40% aq EtOH and dried. 1,1'-Biphenyl
(a). 1,1'-Biphenyl (z). 4-Methyl-1,1'-biphenyl (c). z: M.p. 68.1-69.1 °C;
1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): 7.61 (d, J = 7.1, 4H, H-2), 7.46 (t, J =7.5, 4H,
H-3), 7.36 (t, J =7.4, 2H, H-4). 13C NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3): 141.71,
129.21, 127.70, 127.63. c: M.p. 46.7-47 °C (Ref.3 46-48 °C). 1H NMR (400
MHz, CDCl3): 7.59 (d, J = 7.1, 2H, H-2´), 7.50 (d, J = 8.1, 2H, H-3´),
7.43 (t, J = 7.6, 2H, H-2), 7.33 (t, J = 7.4, 1H, H-3), 7.26 (d, J = 7.9,
2H, H-1´), 2.40 (s, 3H, CH3). 13C NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3): 141.63, 138.83,
137.48, 129.94, 129.21, 129.17, 127.46, 127.44, 127.42, 21.56.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM products depend on catalyst used, Suzuki-Miyaura cross-coupling reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Modular Approach to Heterogenous Catalysis. Manipulation of
Cross-Coupling Catalyst Activity
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
